  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/model_routing.py `run_claude_sandboxed` calls `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"dp-sandboxed-claude-\")`. It then raises `RoutingError` on a `prepare_sandboxed_checkout` failure or a `SandboxedWriterError` (non-macOS, missing srt, CLI or token) without cleaning up. `dispatch_claude_sandboxed` only calls `shutil.rmtree(run[\"workdir\"])` for the `completed` outcome. Each pre-launch refusal therefore leaves a `dp-sandboxed-claude-*` temp directory behind. Before a refusal after checkout preparation, that directory can already hold a full task copy. It holds no token, since the profile is written only after the token is read, so this is a hygiene issue rather than a containment one.",
      "id": "sandboxed-dispatch-workdir-leak-on-refusal",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The disposable workdir is not removed when the sandboxed dispatch fails before or around launch. Retention of a failed run's workdir for diagnosis is documented, but retention on a pre-launch refusal is not."
    }
  ],
